    <item>
      <title>Breadcrumbs</title>
      <link>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/breadcrumbs/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/breadcrumbs/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Breadcrumb paths are a single line of links (often placed above the title) that show a page&amp;rsquo;s location in the site hierarchy. Every website should have breadcrumbs, as it benefits SEO as well as the users understanding of the sites structure. See in action on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/elements/&#34;&gt;Elements page&lt;/a&gt;. To show the breadcrumbs, write the following &amp;lsquo;code&amp;rsquo;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;{{&amp;lt; breadcrumbs &amp;gt;}}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;!--&lt;ul class=&#34;breadcrumbs&#34;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/&#34;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/&#34;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/breadcrumbs/&#34;&gt;Shortcodes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xD;&#xA;--&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Button</title>
      <link>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/button/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/button/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Buttons are a great way to drive conversion. They are actually links with the class &amp;lsquo;button&amp;rsquo;. You can see them in action on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/elements/&#34;&gt;Elements page&lt;/a&gt;. To show a button, write the following &amp;lsquo;code&amp;rsquo;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;{{&amp;lt; button &amp;#34;Get started for free&amp;#34; &amp;#34;/get-started/&amp;#34; &amp;gt;}}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;!--&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/get-started/&#34; class=&#34;button&#34; title=&#34;Get started for free&#34;&gt;Get started for free&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;--&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Contact buttons</title>
      <link>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/contactbuttons/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/contactbuttons/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Contact buttons offer a quick and visual way to contact the site owner. The settings for these buttons can be found in the &amp;lsquo;contact&amp;rsquo; section of the &amp;lsquo;general.yaml&amp;rsquo; file in the data directory. You can see the contact buttons in action on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/elements/&#34;&gt;Elements page&lt;/a&gt;. To show the contact buttons, write the following shortcode:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;{{&amp;lt; contactbuttons &amp;gt;}}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;!--&#xD;&#xA;&lt;ul class=&#34;buttons&#34;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;tel:&amp;#43;31618518928&#34; class=&#34;button icon&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/img/phone.svg&#34; alt=&#34;&amp;#43;31 618 51 89 28&#34; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;mailto:joost@vdschee.nl&#34; class=&#34;button icon&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/img/email.svg&#34; alt=&#34;joost@vdschee.nl&#34; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;--&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Contact form</title>
      <link>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/contact-form/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/contact-form/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The contact form is an essential part for your websites conversion. The settings for this form can be found in the &amp;lsquo;contactform.yaml&amp;rsquo; file in the data directory. You can see the form in action on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/elements/&#34;&gt;Elements page&lt;/a&gt;. To show the contact form in your content, write the following shortcode:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;{{&amp;lt; contactform &amp;gt;}}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;!--&lt;img src=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/form.php&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; opacity: 0; pointer-events: none;&#34; /&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;form id=&#34;contactform&#34; class=&#34;form&#34; method=&#34;POST&#34; action=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/form.php&#34;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Tell us a bit about yourself&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;label class=&#34;inborder&#34; for=&#34;name&#34;&gt;Name&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; name=&#34;name&#34; id=&#34;name&#34; class=&#34;form-control&#34;  required&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;label class=&#34;inborder&#34; for=&#34;email&#34;&gt;Email address&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;input type=&#34;email&#34; name=&#34;email&#34; id=&#34;email&#34; class=&#34;form-control&#34;  required&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;label class=&#34;inborder&#34; for=&#34;message&#34;&gt;Message&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;textarea name=&#34;message&#34; name=&#34;message&#34; id=&#34;message&#34; cols=&#34;30&#34; rows=&#34;10&#34; class=&#34;form-control&#34;  required&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;checkbox&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;label&gt;&lt;input type=&#34;checkbox&#34; name=&#34;terms&#34; value=&#34;I accept the terms and conditions&#34; required&gt;I accept the terms and conditions&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;submit&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;div&gt;&lt;input type=&#34;submit&#34; value=&#34;Submit form&#34; class=&#34;button&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/form&gt;--&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>CTA form</title>
      <link>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/cta-form/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/docs/shortcodes/cta-form/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;A CTA (call to action) form is an essential part for your websites conversion. The settings for this form can be found in the &amp;lsquo;ctaform.yaml&amp;rsquo; file in the data directory. You can see the form in action on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/elements/&#34;&gt;Elements page&lt;/a&gt;. To show the contact form in your content, write the following shortcode:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;{{&amp;lt; ctaform &amp;gt;}}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;!--&lt;img src=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/form.php&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; opacity: 0; pointer-events: none;&#34; /&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;form id=&#34;contactform&#34; class=&#34;form&#34; method=&#34;POST&#34; action=&#34;https://www.hugobricks.preview.usecue.com/form.php&#34;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Enter your details below&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;label class=&#34;inborder&#34; for=&#34;name&#34;&gt;Name&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; name=&#34;name&#34; id=&#34;name&#34; class=&#34;form-control&#34;  required&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;label class=&#34;inborder&#34; for=&#34;email&#34;&gt;Email address&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;input type=&#34;email&#34; name=&#34;email&#34; id=&#34;email&#34; class=&#34;form-control&#34;  required&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;label class=&#34;inborder&#34; for=&#34;message&#34;&gt;Message&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;textarea name=&#34;message&#34; name=&#34;message&#34; id=&#34;message&#34; cols=&#34;30&#34; rows=&#34;10&#34; class=&#34;form-control&#34;  required&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;checkbox&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;label&gt;&lt;input type=&#34;checkbox&#34; name=&#34;terms&#34; value=&#34;I accept the terms and conditions&#34; required&gt;I accept the terms and conditions&lt;/label&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;submit&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;                &lt;div&gt;&lt;input type=&#34;submit&#34; value=&#34;Submit form&#34; class=&#34;button&#34; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;            &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/form&gt;--&gt;</description>
    </item>
